{"id":"mahabharata-7-025","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":25,"title":"पञ्चविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 25 · Bhagadatta attacks Bhima","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how the Pandavas fought when they returned in groups. Bhagadatta on his great elephant, like Indra on Airavata, drives the Pandavas before him and charges Bhima.","kn":"ಗುಂಪುಗುಂಪಾಗಿ ಮರಳಿದ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಹೇಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡಿದರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಐರಾವತದ ಮೇಲಿನ ಇಂದ್ರನಂತೆ ಮಹಾಗಜದ ಮೇಲಿರುವ ಭಗದತ್ತ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಭೀಮನ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि टुकड़ियों में लौटे पाण्डव कैसे लड़े। ऐरावत पर इन्द्र की तरह महागज पर बैठा भगदत्त पाण्डवों को खदेड़ता है और भीम पर टूटता है।","te":"గుంపులుగా తిరిగివచ్చిన పాండవులు ఎలా పోరాడారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. ఐరావతంపై ఇంద్రునిలా మహాగజంపై భగదత్తుడు పాండవులను తరిమి భీమునిపై దూకుతాడు.","ta":"கூட்டம் கூட்டமாகத் திரும்பிய பாண்டவர் எவ்வாறு போரிட்டனர் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். ஐராவதத்தின் மேல் இந்திரன் போல் பெருயானை மீது பகதத்தன் பாண்டவரை விரட்டிப் பீமனைத் தாக்குகிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ സംഘങ്ങളായി മടങ്ങിവന്നപ്പോൾ എങ്ങനെ പൊരുതിയെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ഐരാവതത്തിലെ ഇന്ദ്രനെപ്പോലെ മഹാഗജത്തിൽ ഭഗദത്തൻ പാണ്ഡവരെ തന്റെ മുന്നിലേക്ക് ഓടിക്കുകയും ഭീമനെ ആക്രമിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.25; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संशप्तकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Samshaptakavadha Parva (Slaying of the Samshaptakas)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तेष्वेवं संनिवृत्तेषु प्रत्युद्यातेषु भागशः ।\nकथं युयुधिरे पार्था मामकाश्च तरस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had turned back like that and advanced in separate groups, how did the Parthas and my mighty men fight?"}},{"n":2,"text":"किमर्जुनश्चाप्यकरोत्संशप्तकबलं प्रति ।\nसंशप्तका वा पार्थस्य किमकुर्वत संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"And what did Arjuna do against the host of Samshaptakas, or what did the Samshaptakas do to Partha, Sanjaya?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा तेषु निवृत्तेषु प्रत्युद्यातेषु भागशः ।\nस्वयमभ्यद्रवद्भीमं नागानीकेन ते सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they had turned back and advanced in separate groups, your son himself rushed at Bhima with a division of elephants."}},{"n":4,"text":"स नाग इव नागेन गोवृषेणेव गोवृषः ।\nसमाहूतः स्वयं राज्ञा नागानीकमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like an elephant against an elephant, or a bull against a bull, Bhima, challenged by the king himself, charged the elephant division."}},{"n":5,"text":"स युद्धकुशलः पार्थो बाहुवीर्येण चान्वितः ।\nअभिनत्कुञ्जरानीकमचिरेणैव मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in war and endowed with strength of arm, Partha broke up the elephant force in no time, O sir."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते गजा गिरिसंकाशाः क्षरन्तः सर्वतो मदम् ।\nभीमसेनस्य नाराचैर्विमुखा विमदीकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those elephants, huge as mountains and streaming rut-fluid on all sides, were turned away and robbed of their rut by Bhimasena's iron arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"विधमेदभ्रजालानि यथा वायुः समन्ततः ।\nव्यधमत्तान्यनीकानि तथैव पवनात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the wind scatters masses of cloud on every side, so the son of the Wind scattered those divisions."}},{"n":8,"text":"स तेषु विसृजन्बाणान्भीमो नागेष्वशोभत ।\nभुवनेष्विव सर्वेषु गभस्तीनुदितो रविः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Loosing his arrows among those elephants, Bhima shone like the risen sun scattering its rays over all the worlds."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते भीमबाणैः शतशः संस्यूता विबभुर्गजाः ।\nगभस्तिभिरिवार्कस्य व्योम्नि नानाबलाहकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced through by hundreds of Bhima's arrows, the elephants looked like many clouds in the sky pierced by sunbeams."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथा गजानां कदनं कुर्वाणमनिलात्मजम् ।\nक्रुद्धो दुर्योधनोऽभ्येत्य प्रत्यविध्यच्छितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Wind's son was slaughtering the elephants, angry Duryodhana came up and pierced him with sharp arrows."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः क्षणेन क्षितिपं क्षतजप्रतिमेक्षणः ।\nक्षयं निनीषुर्निशितैर्भीमो विव्याध पत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in a moment Bhima, his eyes red as blood, wishing to destroy the king, pierced him with sharp feathered arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"स शरार्पितसर्वाङ्गः क्रुद्धो विव्याध पाण्डवम् ।\nनाराचैरर्करश्म्याभैर्भीमसेनं स्मयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His whole body struck by arrows, Duryodhana in anger pierced Bhimasena with iron arrows like sunbeams, almost smiling."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्य नागं मणिमयं रत्नचित्रं ध्वजे स्थितम् ।\nभल्लाभ्यां कार्मुकं चैव क्षिप्रं चिच्छेद पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava swiftly cut down with two broad-headed arrows the jeweled elephant on his banner, wonderfully set with gems, and his bow too."}},{"n":14,"text":"दुर्योधनं पीड्यमानं दृष्ट्वा भीमेन मारिष ।\nचुक्षोभयिषुरभ्यागादङ्गो मातङ्गमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Duryodhana hard pressed by Bhima, O sir, Anga, mounted on an elephant, came up wishing to throw Bhima into confusion."}},{"n":15,"text":"तमापतन्तं मातङ्गमम्बुदप्रतिमस्वनम् ।\nकुम्भान्तरे भीमसेनो नाराचेनार्दयद्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that elephant, thundering like a cloud, charged, Bhimasena struck it hard between the temples with an iron arrow."}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्य कायं विनिर्भिद्य ममज्ज धरणीतले ।\nततः पपात द्विरदो वज्राहत इवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrow pierced its body and sank into the ground, and the elephant fell like a mountain struck by a thunderbolt."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्यावर्जितनागस्य म्लेच्छस्यावपतिष्यतः ।\nशिरश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन क्षिप्रकारी वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that barbarian Anga fell from his overturned elephant, quick Vrikodara cut off his head with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मिन्निपतिते वीरे संप्राद्रवत सा चमूः ।\nसंभ्रान्ताश्वद्विपरथा पदातीनवमृद्नती ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that hero fell, his army fled, its horses, elephants and chariots confused, trampling its own foot soldiers."}},{"n":19,"text":"तेष्वनीकेषु सर्वेषु विद्रवत्सु समन्ततः ।\nप्राग्ज्योतिषस्ततो भीमं कुञ्जरेण समाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While all those divisions were fleeing in every direction, Pragjyotisha, Bhagadatta, charged at Bhima on his elephant."}},{"n":20,"text":"येन नागेन मघवानजयद्दैत्यदानवान् ।\nस नागप्रवरो भीमं सहसा समुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That excellent elephant, on which Indra had conquered the Daityas and Danavas, rushed suddenly at Bhima."}},{"n":21,"text":"श्रवणाभ्यामथो पद्भ्यां संहतेन करेण च ।\nव्यावृत्तनयनः क्रुद्धः प्रदहन्निव पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With ears, feet and its curled trunk, rolling its eyes in rage, it seemed to burn up the Pandava."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः सर्वस्य सैन्यस्य नादः समभवन्महान् ।\nहा हा विनिहतो भीमः कुञ्जरेणेति मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great cry rose from all the army: \"Alas, alas, Bhima is killed by the elephant!\" O sir."}},{"n":23,"text":"तेन नादेन वित्रस्ता पाण्डवानामनीकिनी ।\nसहसाभ्यद्रवद्राजन्यत्र तस्थौ वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified by that cry, the Pandava army suddenly rushed toward where Vrikodara stood, O king."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा हतं मत्वा वृकोदरम् ।\nभगदत्तं सपाञ्चालः सर्वतः समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, thinking Vrikodara slain, surrounded Bhagadatta on every side with the Panchalas."}},{"n":25,"text":"तं रथै रथिनां श्रेष्ठाः परिवार्य समन्ततः ।\nअवाकिरञ्शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of chariot-warriors encircled him with their chariots and showered him with sharp arrows by the hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":26,"text":"स विघातं पृषत्कानामङ्कुशेन समाचरन् ।\nगजेन पाण्डुपाञ्चालान्व्यधमत्पर्वतेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Using his goad to ward off the arrows, the mountain king Bhagadatta on his elephant crushed the Pandavas and Panchalas."}},{"n":27,"text":"तदद्भुतमपश्याम भगदत्तस्य संयुगे ।\nतथा वृद्धस्य चरितं कुञ्जरेण विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw that marvelous deed of Bhagadatta in battle, O lord of men, the exploit of that old man on his elephant."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो राजा दशार्णानां प्राग्ज्योतिषमुपाद्रवत् ।\nतिर्यग्यातेन नागेन समदेनाशुगामिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king of the Dasharnas charged Pragjyotisha with a swift, rutting elephant, moving sideways."}},{"n":29,"text":"तयोर्युद्धं समभवन्नागयोर्भीमरूपयोः ।\nसपक्षयोः पर्वतयोर्यथा सद्रुमयोः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The battle between those two terrible elephants was like that of two winged, tree-covered mountains in ancient times."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषपतेर्नागः संनिपत्यापवृत्य च ।\nपार्श्वे दशार्णाधिपतेर्भित्त्वा नागमपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pragjyotisha's elephant charged, wheeled, and gored the side of the Dasharna king's elephant, bringing it down."}},{"n":31,"text":"तोमरैः सूर्यरश्म्याभैर्भगदत्तोऽथ सप्तभिः ।\nजघान द्विरदस्थं तं शत्रुं प्रचलितासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta then killed that enemy, riding his elephant with his seat shaken, with seven lances bright as sunbeams."}},{"n":32,"text":"उपसृत्य तु राजानं भगदत्तं युधिष्ठिरः ।\nरथानीकेन महता सर्वतः पर्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira approached King Bhagadatta and surrounded him on all sides with a great division of chariots."}},{"n":33,"text":"स कुञ्जरस्थो रथिभिः शुशुभे सर्वतो वृतः ।\nपर्वते वनमध्यस्थो ज्वलन्निव हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by chariot-warriors, he shone mounted on his elephant, like a blazing fire in the middle of a forest on a mountain."}},{"n":34,"text":"मण्डलं सर्वतः श्लिष्टं रथिनामुग्रधन्विनाम् ।\nकिरतां शरवर्षाणि स नागः पर्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That elephant circled round the closely packed ring of fierce-bowed chariot-warriors showering arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः प्राग्ज्योतिषो राजा परिगृह्य द्विपर्षभम् ।\nप्रेषयामास सहसा युयुधानरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Pragjyotisha, taking hold of his best of elephants, suddenly sent it at Yuyudhana's chariot."}},{"n":36,"text":"शिनेः पौत्रस्य तु रथं परिगृह्य महाद्विपः ।\nअभिचिक्षेप वेगेन युयुधानस्त्वपाक्रमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great elephant seized the chariot of Shini's grandson and hurled it with speed, but Yuyudhana had slipped away."}},{"n":37,"text":"बृहतः सैन्धवानश्वान्समुत्थाप्य तु सारथिः ।\nतस्थौ सात्यकिमासाद्य संप्लुतस्तं रथं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The charioteer raised the great Sindhu horses and stood again, leaping back into that chariot beside Satyaki."}},{"n":38,"text":"स तु लब्ध्वान्तरं नागस्त्वरितो रथमण्डलात् ।\nनिश्चक्राम ततः सर्वान्परिचिक्षेप पार्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephant, finding its opening, swiftly came out of the ring of chariots and encircled all the kings."}},{"n":39,"text":"ते त्वाशुगतिना तेन त्रास्यमाना नरर्षभाः ।\nतमेकं द्विरदं संख्ये मेनिरे शतशो नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified by that swift-moving beast, those best of men, those kings, thought that one elephant in battle was hundreds."}},{"n":40,"text":"ते गजस्थेन काल्यन्ते भगदत्तेन पाण्डवाः ।\nऐरावतस्थेन यथा देवराजेन दानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas were driven by Bhagadatta on his elephant as the Danavas were driven by the king of the gods on Airavata."}},{"n":41,"text":"तेषां प्रद्रवतां भीमः पाञ्चालानामितस्ततः ।\nगजवाजिकृतः शब्दः सुमहान्समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Panchalas fled here and there, a great noise of elephants and horses arose."}},{"n":42,"text":"भगदत्तेन समरे काल्यमानेषु पाण्डुषु ।\nप्राग्ज्योतिषमभिक्रुद्धः पुनर्भीमः समभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas were being driven by Bhagadatta, Bhima again advanced in fury against Pragjyotisha."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्याभिद्रवतो वाहान्हस्तमुक्तेन वारिणा ।\nसिक्त्वा व्यत्रासयन्नागस्ते पार्थमहरंस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephant, sprinkling water from its trunk on the horses of Bhima's chariot as he rushed at it, frightened them, and they carried Partha away."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततस्तमभ्ययात्तूर्णं रुचिपर्वाकृतीसुतः ।\nसमुक्षञ्शरवर्षेण रथस्थोऽन्तकसंनिभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ruchiparva, the son of Akriti, riding in his chariot like Death, quickly attacked, showering arrows."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततो रुचिरपर्वाणं शरेण नतपर्वणा ।\nसुपर्वा पर्वतपतिर्निन्ये वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mountain king Bhagadatta, with a bent-jointed arrow, sent Ruchiparva to Yama's abode."}},{"n":46,"text":"तस्मिन्निपतिते वीरे सौभद्रो द्रौपदीसुताः ।\nचेकितानो धृष्टकेतुर्युयुत्सुश्चार्दयन्द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that hero fell, Subhadra's son, Draupadi's sons, Chekitana, Dhrishtaketu and Yuyutsu attacked the elephant."}},{"n":47,"text":"त एनं शरधाराभिर्धाराभिरिव तोयदाः ।\nसिषिचुर्भैरवान्नादान्विनदन्तो जिघांसवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They poured streams of arrows on it, like clouds pouring rain, roaring terrible cries and wishing to kill it."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः पार्ष्ण्यङ्कुशाङ्गुष्ठैः कृतिना चोदितो द्विपः ।\nप्रसारितकरः प्रायात्स्तब्धकर्णेक्षणो द्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, urged by its skilled rider with heel, goad and toe, the elephant rushed on swiftly, trunk outstretched, ears and eyes fixed."}},{"n":49,"text":"सोऽधिष्ठाय पदा वाहान्युयुत्सोः सूतमारुजत् ।\nपुत्रस्तु तव संभ्रान्तः सौभद्रस्याप्लुतो रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With its foot it crushed the horses of Yuyutsu and broke his charioteer; your son, confused, leapt into Subhadra's son's chariot."}},{"n":50,"text":"स कुञ्जरस्थो विसृजन्निषूनरिषु पार्थिवः ।\nबभौ रश्मीनिवादित्यो भुवनेषु समुत्सृजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king on his elephant, loosing arrows at his enemies, shone like the sun releasing its rays over the worlds."}},{"n":51,"text":"तमार्जुनिर्द्वादशभिर्युयुत्सुर्दशभिः शरैः ।\nत्रिभिस्त्रिभिर्द्रौपदेया धृष्टकेतुश्च विव्यधुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu pierced him with twelve arrows, Yuyutsu with ten, and each of Draupadi's sons and Dhrishtaketu with three."}},{"n":52,"text":"सोऽरियत्नार्पितैर्बाणैराचितो द्विरदो बभौ ।\nसंस्यूत इव सूर्यस्य रश्मिभिर्जलदो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stuck all over with arrows aimed by his enemies, the elephant shone like a great cloud pierced by sunbeams."}},{"n":53,"text":"नियन्तुः शिल्पयत्नाभ्यां प्रेषितोऽरिशरार्दितः ।\nपरिचिक्षेप तान्नागः स रिपून्सव्यदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by the skill and effort of its rider, tormented by enemy arrows, that elephant circled the foes to left and right."}},{"n":54,"text":"गोपाल इव दण्डेन यथा पशुगणान्वने ।\nआवेष्टयत तां सेनां भगदत्तस्तथा मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a herdsman with his staff gathers cattle in the forest, so Bhagadatta again and again rounded up that army."}},{"n":55,"text":"क्षिप्रं श्येनाभिपन्नानां वायसानामिव स्वनः ।\nबभूव पाण्डवेयानां भृशं विद्रवतां स्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A loud cry rose swiftly from the fleeing Pandava forces, like the cry of crows swooped upon by hawks."}},{"n":56,"text":"स नागराजः प्रवराङ्कुशाहतः\nपुरा सपक्षोऽद्रिवरो यथा नृप ।\nभयं तथा रिपुषु समादधद्भृशं\nवणिग्गणानां क्षुभितो यथार्णवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by its best goad, that king of elephants spread great fear among the enemy, as a winged mountain once did, as a stormy sea does merchants."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततो ध्वनिर्द्विरदरथाश्वपार्थिवै-\nर्भयाद्द्रवद्भिर्जनितोऽतिभैरवः ।\nक्षितिं वियद्द्यां विदिशो दिशस्तथा\nसमावृणोत्पार्थिव संयुगे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a dreadful din rose from elephants, chariots, horses and kings fleeing in terror, filling the earth, sky and all directions in that battle, O king."}},{"n":58,"text":"स तेन नागप्रवरेण पार्थिवो\nभृशं जगाहे द्विषतामनीकिनीम् ।\nपुरा सुगुप्तां विबुधैरिवाहवे\nविरोचनो देववरूथिनीमिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that best of elephants the king plunged deeply into the enemy army, as Virochana once plunged into the host of the gods, well guarded in battle."}},{"n":59,"text":"भृशं ववौ ज्वलनसखो वियद्रजः\nसमावृणोन्मुहुरपि चैव सैनिकान् ।\nतमेकनागं गणशो यथा गजाः\nसमन्ततो द्रुतमिव मेनिरे जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dust, friend of fire, blew thick and covered the soldiers again and again; and the people thought that one elephant was many, rushing at them everywhere."}}]}]}